evaluate(t) → {sR,dR,sB,dB, vR,aR, vB,aB} where v = ds/dt, a = d²s/dt² (derivatives of the PCHIP, analytic). I'll compute the derivative analytically from the Hermite basis:
For interval i with h=1, u = (t - x_i)/h:
s(t) = h00*y_i + h10*h*m_i + h01*y_{i+1} + h11*h*m_{i+1}
h00 = 2u³-3u²+1, h10 = u³-2u²+u, h01 = -2u³+3u², h11 = u³-u²
ds/dt = (1/h) * [h00'*y_i + h10'*h*m_i + h01'*y_{i+1} + h11'*h*m_{i+1}]
h00' = 6u²-6u, h10' = 3u²-4u+1, h01' = -6u²+6u, h11' = 3u²-2u
d²s/dt² = (1/h²) * [h00''*y_i + h10''*h*m_i + h01''*y_{i+1} + h11''*h*m_{i+1}]
h00'' = 12u-6, h10'' = 6u-4, h01'' = -12u+6, h11'' = 6u-2

